2026-05-15 02:29:15,249 - INFO - GenAIOps Result: {'answer': "Insurance benefits for insured credit cards are managed through a specific authorization and settlement process involving Techcombank and the insurance company. \n\n- **Authorization**: The primary cardholder authorizes Techcombank to receive all insurance benefits on their behalf during the validity of the credit card and insurance policy. This authorization cannot be amended or terminated during the policy's validity (according to Section 10.3).\n  \n- **Debt Settlement**: If an insurance event occurs, Techcombank will use the insurance benefits to pay any outstanding debts the primary cardholder has with Techcombank. If the insurance benefits are insufficient to cover the debts, the cardholder remains responsible for repaying the remaining amount, including any fees and interest (according to Section 10.2).\n\n- **Excess Benefits**: If the insurance benefits exceed the debts owed, Techcombank will refund the remaining amount to the primary cardholder in accordance with its provisions and the law (according to Section 10.2).\n\n- **Notification Requirement**: The cardholder must notify Techcombank or the insurance company within 30 days of the occurrence of an insurance event to initiate the settlement of benefits (according to Section 10.4).\n\nFor any specific details or confirmation, please refer to the official support channel of the bank.", 'context': '[Source] debts that the Primary Cardholder of the insured credit card must pay to \n\nTechcombank, Techcombank is responsible for refunding the remaining insurance benefits in accordance \n\nwith the provisions of Techcombank and the law. \n\n10.3. AUTHORIZATION TO RECEIVE INSURANCE BENEFITS \n\nIn case the insurance company settles the insurance benefits when the insurance event occurs, the primary \n\ncardholder of the insured credit card agrees to authorize Techcombank to receive all these insurance benefits \n\non behalf of the primary cardholder of the insured credit card with the following agreements: \n\n\n\n     \n\n \n\nCode: MB01-QĐ2.CARD/03      Promulgation/Revision: 1.1  Page number: 19/21 \n\na. This authorization is valid during the credit card validity period and throughout the validity period of the \n\ninsurance policy in relation to each primary cardholder of the insured credit card; \n\nb. This authorization may not be amended, supplemented, replaced, canceled, or terminated during the validity \n\nperiod of the insurance policy related to each primary cardholder of the insured credit card. \n\nc. Techcombank is entitled to use this Insurance Benefit to pay debts that the Primary Cardholder of the \n\ninsured credit card has not paid to Techcombank (if any). After deducting the debts, if the insurance benefits \n\nare insufficient compared to the debts that the Insured Credit Card Cardholder must pay to Techcombank, \n\nthe Insured Credit Card Cardholder is responsible for continuing to make full and timely debt repayment \n\nand payment of fees,  interest incurred (if any); if the insurance benefits are more than the debts that the \n\nPrimary Cardholder of the insured credit card must pay to Techcombank, Techcombank shall be responsible \n\nfor reimbursing the Principal Cardholder of the insured credit card the remaining amount in accordance with \n\nthe provisions of Techcombank and the law.\n\n---\n\n[Source] pay to Techcombank, \n\nthe Insured Credit Card Cardholder is responsible for continuing to make full and timely debt repayment \n\nand payment of fees,  interest incurred (if any); if the insurance benefits are more than the debts that the \n\nPrimary Cardholder of the insured credit card must pay to Techcombank, Techcombank shall be responsible \n\nfor reimbursing the Principal Cardholder of the insured credit card the remaining amount in accordance with \n\nthe provisions of Techcombank and the law. \n\nd. In order to settle the outstanding debts of the credit cardholder, Techcombank reserves the right to \n\ntemporarily lock/block the account of the primary cardholder in case of necessity. \n\n10.4. SETTLEMENT OF INSURANCE BENEFITS \n\na. In case an insurance event occurs and falls within the coverage of the insurance contract issued to the \n\nPrimary Cardholder of the insured credit card, the Claimant must notify Techcombank or the Insurance \n\nCompany, within 30 days from the occurrence of the insurance event. Techcombank and the Insurance \n\nCompany are responsible for coordinating to settle insurance benefits for the Claimant according to the \n\nagreement between Techcombank and the Insurance Company. \n\nb. Techcombank and the Insurance Company are independently responsible for the main cardholder of the \n\ninsured credit card in exercising their rights and obligations. Techcombank is not responsible for \n\nanswering/settling complaints from Cardholders related to the performance of insurance obligations of the \n\nInsurance Company. \n\n11. OTHER TERMS  \n\n11.1. OTHER REGULATIONS \n\na. If the Cardholder uses the Card to reserve services but does not use such services and does not notify the \n\ncancellation of the service within the time limit specified by the Cardholder, the Cardholder may have to \n\npay part or all of the service value, relevant taxes and fees as prescribed by each Merchant. Techcombank \n\nreserves the right to debit the Cardholder\'s Account in these cases. \n\nb.\n\n---\n\n[Source] credit card will become the Insured Person according to the type of insurance product purchased by \n\nTechcombank from time to time. \n\nc. In case of arising risks under the insurer\'s insurance liability, the primary cardholder of the insured credit \n\ncard agrees to let Techcombank become the beneficiary/beneficiary of the insurance benefit. Techcombank \n\nwill use this Insurance Benefit to pay debts that the Cardholder has not paid to Techcombank (if any). \n\n10.2. DESIGNATION OF BENEFICIARIES   \n\nTechcombank and the Primary Cardholder of the Insured Credit Card mutually agree to designate \n\nTechcombank as the first beneficiary in the event that the insurance event occurs to the Primary Cardholder \n\ncovered by the insurance product, and will not sue the Insurer after the insurance benefits are paid to \n\nTechcombank by the Insurer. Accordingly, the insurance company will pay the insurance benefit to \n\nTechcombank and Techcombank is entitled to use this insurance benefit to pay the debts that the main \n\ncardholder of the insured credit card has not paid to Techcombank (if any). After deduction of debts, if the \n\ninsurance benefits are insufficient compared to the debts that the primary cardholder of the insured credit \n\ncard must pay to Techcombank, the responsibility to continue to repay the debt in full and on time and pay \n\nthe arising fees and interests (if any) shall comply with the provisions of Techcombank and the law; if the \n\ninsurance benefits are more than the debts that the Primary Cardholder of the insured credit card must pay to \n\nTechcombank, Techcombank is responsible for refunding the remaining insurance benefits in accordance \n\nwith the provisions of Techcombank and the law. \n\n10.3. AUTHORIZATION TO RECEIVE INSURANCE BENEFITS \n\nIn case the insurance company settles the insurance benefits when the insurance event occurs, the primary \n\ncardholder of the insured credit card agrees to authorize Techcombank to receive all these insurance benefits\n\n---\n\n[Source] through the following methods, including but not limited to \n\nthe Cardholder\'s direct phone call to Techcombank (only applicable to cases of telephone assistance \n\naccording to Techcombank\'s internal regulations from time to time),  Cardholders directly go to \n\nTechcombank\'s branches/transaction offices, cardholders directly register via i-bank/F@stMobile F@st, etc. \n\nThe Cardholder must take all responsibility for the services that the Cardholder requests from Techcombank \n\nto change. \n\nr. Agree for Techcombank to confirm all or part of the online card payment transaction in case of using the \n\nconfirmation form for online card payment transaction according to EMV 3-D Secure standard. The online \n\ncard transaction confirmation will be in accordance with Techcombank\'s relevant regulations from time to \n\ntime. \n\n10. INSURANCE-RELATED REGULATIONS FOR INSURED CREDIT CARDS \n\n10.1. COMMITMENT OF THE MAIN CARDHOLDER OF THE INSURED CREDIT CARD: \n\na. Agree to allow Techcombank, doctors, medical organizations and other relevant organizations and \n\nindividuals to provide the insurance company and reinsurance companies with information related to the \n\nperformance of the insurance contract concluded on the basis of the application for issuance of an \n\ninternational credit card card use contract. \n\nb. After successfully opening the Card, depending on the type of Card, the main cardholder of the insured \n\ncredit card will become the Insured Person according to the type of insurance product purchased by \n\nTechcombank from time to time. \n\nc. In case of arising risks under the insurer\'s insurance liability, the primary cardholder of the insured credit \n\ncard agrees to let Techcombank become the beneficiary/beneficiary of the insurance benefit. Techcombank \n\nwill use this Insurance Benefit to pay debts that the Cardholder has not paid to Techcombank (if any). \n\n10.2. DESIGNATION OF BENEFICIARIES\n\n---\n\n[Source] regulations, \n\nwhich is accepted by Techcombank as collateral for the use of the Cardholder\'s Credit Limit and is not used \n\nfor payment in statement periods. \n\n1.1.28 "Insurance company": means a company that provides insurance products in accordance with the \n\nprovisions of Vietnamese law. \n\n1.1.29 "Insurance Product": means a product provided by the Insurance Company to Techcombank in \n\naccordance with the insurance rules approved and licensed by the Ministry of Finance, and purchased by \n\nTechcombank as a gift to the Primary Cardholder of the insured credit card. The purchase of insurance \n\n\n\n     \n\n \n\nCode: MB01-QĐ2.CARD/03      Promulgation/Revision: 1.1  Page number: 3/21 \n\nproducts of a specific insurance company by Techcombank to give to the Primary Cardholder of the insured \n\ncredit card will be announced by Techcombank on Techcombank\'s official website at each specific time.  \n\n1.1.30 "Transaction processing date of the International Card Organization": means the date on which the \n\nInternational Card Organization processes transactions transferred by card-accepting units to the system of \n\nthe International Card Organization. \n\n1.1.31 "Request via Call Center": means the main cardholder\'s request for assistance through the Call Center, \n\nwhereby the main cardholder is responsible for correctly answering the cardholder\'s authentication \n\nquestions according to Techcombank\'s regulations to be processed by the call center. Techcombank has the \n\nright to process the request of an individual calling the Call Center if the individual correctly answers the \n\npassword of the telephone transaction in accordance with Techcombank\'s regulations and Techcombank is \n\nexempt from responsibility for processing this request in case the Cardholder discloses the password of the \n\nCardholder\'s telephone transaction to a third party. \n\n1.1.32 "Call Center": Techcombank\'s 24/7 Customer Service Call Center and any other telephone'}
